<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
  arch_ethereal.xml — VPR architecture description for the Ethereal fabric
  =======================================================================
  Task:        E0-MAP2 (VPR 架构文件, eLUT4 cluster + W=12)
  Plan-Ref:    ethereal-plan/components/C-soft-工具与固件组件.md §2 (bitgen 两级)
               ethereal-plan/components/C01-fabric-核心单元.md §3 (CLB-T / SB / CB)
  Maintainer:  BaiTian6641
  Created:     2026-07-25

  === What this models ===
  A VPR island-style architecture that mirrors the IMPLEMENTED Ethereal fabric
  (ethereal-fabric/rtl/) so VPR can pack/place/route a netlist (from synth_ethereal,
  E0-MAP1) onto it. The routing solution (rr_graph) is later translated by bitgen
  (E0-MAP3) into fabric config frames via frame_map.json.

    Logic block "clb"      <-> clb_t   : N=8 eLUT4 (BLE = LUT4 + FF + out-mux),
                                                flat full-input crossbar I=EXT_IN=18
                                                (18 ext inputs + 8 local feedback = 26).
                                                [equivalent="full" on I makes VPR's
                                                 packer treat the 18 inputs as a pool,
                                                 matching clb_t's full crossbar.]
    BLE (fle/ble4)         <-> eLUT4   : LUT4 (class lut, .names) + FF (class flipflop,
                                                .latch) + 2:1 output mux (LUT|FF).
                                                eLUT4's output-invert folds into the TT.
    Routing channel        <-> W=12    : supplied as route_chan_width=12 on the CLI.
    Switch block           <-> switch_box (Wilton track-permuting Fs=3, v1.1).
                                                VPR token "wilton": <switch_block type="wilton" fs="3"/>.
                                                (Our Option-B router on the hand-built
                                                fabric is authoritative; this arch is
                                                kept consistent for VPR pack/place parity.)
    Connection block       <-> connection_block (input CB = full mux of 4*W tracks;
                                                output = clb_out -> out_e inject).
    Segment                : length-1 unidir (per-tile SB hop), R/Cmetal ~0 (sim arch).

  === ASSUMPTIONs (G6, TBD 2026-07-25) ===
  A. fc in/out = 0.25/0.25 is a ROUTABILITY approximation, NOT an exact match to
     the implemented CB connectivity (input CB is a full 4*W mux → in_val=1.0 is
     the faithful value; output injects onto out_e only). Exact rr_graph -> mux
     mapping is performed by bitgen (E0-MAP3) using the SB-topology table from
     fabric_gen; this arch only needs to be routable for E0-MAP2's acceptance
     ("VPR pack/place/route on c432, timing report readable").
  B. Timing values are inherited verbatim from VTR's k4_N4_90nm.xml (90nm PTM) so
     the timing report is readable; they are NOT the real Ethereal-fabric delays
     (no silicon/timing-characterization yet — Phase 1+).
  C. switch_block type="wilton" (track-permuting Fs=3) matches the implemented
     switch_box (v1.1, 2026-07-26): a signal changes track index at each SB hop,
     breaking the disjoint track-locking that stranded c432 (E0-MAP3 incr 4a
     Cause 2). The Option-B bitgen router on the hand-built fabric is
     authoritative; this arch token is kept consistent for VPR pack/place parity.
  D. Channel width W=12 is supplied on the CLI; the arch sets no hard chan cap.

  === Heterogeneous extension (Phase-1, Stage 5a, 2026-07-28) ===
  Two new tile pb_types join clb/io so VPR can place the hard cells emitted by
  synth_ethereal's heterogeneous=True flow (memory-> $mem_v2, alumacc-> $macc_v2):

    mult_27x18 (dsp_t)  : 27x18 -> 48-bit multiplier/MAC. Yosys emits it as
                          `.subckt $macc_v2` with ports A[26:0], B[17:0], Y[47:0].
                          blif_model=".subckt $macc_v2"; the matching <model name="$macc_v2">
                          declares those ports (combinational A/B -> Y).
    mem_2Kx32 (mem_t)   : 2K x 32-bit synchronous RAM. Yosys emits it as
                          `.subckt $mem_v2` (NOT VPR's built-in single_port_ram).
                          Real Yosys $mem_v2 is dual-port (RD_*/WR_*), which does
                          NOT match single_port_ram's single-addr model, so the
                          blif_model is `.subckt $mem_v2` + a matching custom
                          <model name="$mem_v2">. class="memory" lets VPR pack it.
  Both are added to <models> (VPR throws "Failed to find matching architecture
  model" for any .subckt name it does not have built-in or declared).

  ASSUMPTIONs for the new tiles (G6, TBD 2026-07-28):
  E. fc in/out = 1.0/1.0 on mult_27x18 & mem_2Kx32. VTR's own wide tiles use
     0.15/0.10, but that left most mult/mem pins with NO rr_graph fanin/fanout
     (VPR check_rr_graph warnings) at our tiny W=12: too few channels brush the
     tall hard columns, so a fractional fc starves the wide pins. fc=1.0 connects
     every hard-tile pin to the channel. Routability approximation only; exact
     rr_graph -> fabric-mux mapping is bitgen's job (E0-MAP3 heterogeneous,
     not yet built).
  F. Column pattern (mult every 4th col from x=4, memory every 5th from x=5)
     is a PLACEHOLDER heterogeneous layout, chosen to give a few hard-tile
     columns without disturbing the clb fill / io perimeter. Real mem_t/dsp_t
     floorplan comes from fabric.yaml in a later phase.
  G. $mem_v2 is modelled as a single-clock synchronous RAM: RD_CLK/WR_CLK both
     connect to the tile's `clk`; RD_EN/WR_EN are synchronous write/read enables
     (clock="clk"); RD_ARST/RD_SRST are bundled into the sync `ctrl` port
     (tie-off in Phase-1 probes — async reset inference is a heterogeneous-
     bitgen concern, deferred). See note in the mem_2Kx32 pb_type.

  Adapted from vtr_flow/arch/timing/k4_N4_90nm.xml (VTR v8.0.0), which is the
  canonical v8.0.0-verified homogeneous LUT4+FF cluster reference. mult/memory
  tile structure follows vtr_flow/arch/timing/EArch.xml + k6_N10_mem32K_40nm.xml.
-->
<architecture>

  <!-- Built-in: .names (LUT) / .input / .output / .latch (FF).
       Custom: $macc_v2 (dsp_t) + $mem_v2 (mem_t) from the heterogeneous synth.
       (VPR has multiply/single_port_ram/dual_port_ram/adder built-in, but Yosys
        emits neither — it emits $macc_v2/$mem_v2, so those are declared here.) -->
  <models>
    <!-- dsp_t: 27x18 -> 48 multiplier/MAC. Pure combinational A/B -> Y
         (the pipelining FFs live in surrounding clbs). -->
    <model name="$macc_v2">
      <input_ports>
        <port name="A" combinational_sink_ports="Y"/>
        <port name="B" combinational_sink_ports="Y"/>
      </input_ports>
      <output_ports>
        <port name="Y"/>
      </output_ports>
    </model>

    <!-- mem_t: 2Kx32 synchronous RAM. Yosys $mem_v2 dual-port form.
         Write side (WR_CLK/WR_EN/WR_ADDR/WR_DATA) + read side
         (RD_CLK/RD_EN/RD_ADDR -> RD_DATA) are all clocked (synchronous). -->
    <model name="$mem_v2">
      <input_ports>
        <port name="WR_CLK"  is_clock="1"/>
        <port name="WR_EN"   clock="WR_CLK"/>
        <port name="WR_ADDR" clock="WR_CLK"/>
        <port name="WR_DATA" clock="WR_CLK"/>
        <port name="RD_CLK"  is_clock="1"/>
        <port name="RD_EN"   clock="RD_CLK"/>
        <port name="RD_ADDR" clock="RD_CLK"/>
        <port name="RD_ARST" clock="RD_CLK"/>
        <port name="RD_SRST" clock="RD_CLK"/>
      </input_ports>
      <output_ports>
        <port name="RD_DATA" clock="RD_CLK"/>
      </output_ports>
    </model>
  </models>

  <!-- Physical layout: io on the perimeter, clb filling the core, with
       hard-tile columns interleaved (mult every 4th col, memory every 5th).
       Each hard column gets an EMPTY filler col (priority one lower) so VPR
       leaves EMPTY wherever a height-1 tile does not fit the perimeter offset.
       Pattern follows VTR's EArch.xml multi-tile <auto_layout>. -->
  <layout>
    <auto_layout aspect_ratio="1.000000">
      <perimeter type="io" priority="100"/>
      <corners type="EMPTY" priority="101"/>
      <fill type="clb" priority="10"/>
      <!-- dsp_t columns (mult every 4th column, offset 1 for the io perimeter) -->
      <col type="mult_27x18" startx="4" starty="1" repeatx="4" priority="20"/>
      <col type="EMPTY"      startx="4" starty="1" repeatx="4" priority="19"/>
      <!-- mem_t columns (memory every 5th column) -->
      <col type="mem_2Kx32" startx="5" starty="1" repeatx="5" priority="20"/>
      <col type="EMPTY"     startx="5" starty="1" repeatx="5" priority="19"/>
    </auto_layout>
  </layout>

  <device>
    <sizing R_minW_nmos="4220.930176" R_minW_pmos="11207.599609"/>
    <area grid_logic_tile_area="2229.320068"/>
    <chan_width_distr>
      <x distr="uniform" peak="1.000000"/>
      <y distr="uniform" peak="1.000000"/>
    </chan_width_distr>
    <switch_block type="wilton" fs="3"/>
    <connection_block input_switch_name="ipin_cblock"/>
  </device>

  <switchlist>
    <switch type="mux" name="0" R="0.000000" Cin="0.000000e+00" Cout="0.000000e+00"
            Tdel="6.244000e-11" mux_trans_size="1.835460" buf_size="10.498600"/>
    <switch type="mux" name="ipin_cblock" R="1055.232544" Cout="0." Cin="0.000000e+00"
            Tdel="8.045000e-11" mux_trans_size="0.983352" buf_size="auto"/>
  </switchlist>

  <segmentlist>
    <segment freq="1.000000" length="1" type="unidir" Rmetal="0.000000" Cmetal="0.000000e+00">
      <mux name="0"/>
      <sb type="pattern">1 1</sb>
      <cb type="pattern">1</cb>
    </segment>
  </segmentlist>

  <complexblocklist>

    <!-- ================= I/O pads (perimeter) ================= -->
    <pb_type name="io" capacity="3">
      <input  name="outpad" num_pins="1"/>
      <output name="inpad"  num_pins="1"/>
      <clock  name="clock"  num_pins="1"/>

      <mode name="inpad">
        <pb_type name="inpad" blif_model=".input" num_pb="1">
          <output name="inpad" num_pins="1"/>
        </pb_type>
        <interconnect>
          <direct name="inpad" input="inpad.inpad" output="io.inpad">
            <delay_constant max="9.492000e-11" in_port="inpad.inpad" out_port="io.inpad"/>
          </direct>
        </interconnect>
      </mode>
      <mode name="outpad">
        <pb_type name="outpad" blif_model=".output" num_pb="1">
          <input name="outpad" num_pins="1"/>
        </pb_type>
        <interconnect>
          <direct name="outpad" input="io.outpad" output="outpad.outpad">
            <delay_constant max="2.675000e-11" in_port="io.outpad" out_port="outpad.outpad"/>
          </direct>
        </interconnect>
      </mode>

      <fc in_type="frac" in_val="1.0" out_type="frac" out_val="0.25"/>
      <pinlocations pattern="custom">
        <loc side="left">io.outpad io.inpad io.clock</loc>
        <loc side="top">io.outpad io.inpad io.clock</loc>
        <loc side="right">io.outpad io.inpad io.clock</loc>
        <loc side="bottom">io.outpad io.inpad io.clock</loc>
      </pinlocations>
      <power method="ignore"/>
    </pb_type>

    <!-- ================= Ethereal CLB (clb_t: N=8 eLUT4) ================= -->
    <pb_type name="clb">
      <!-- I=EXT_IN=18 (full pool — clb_t's flat crossbar); O=N=8 -->
      <input  name="I"   num_pins="18" equivalent="full"/>
      <output name="O"   num_pins="8"  equivalent="instance"/>
      <clock  name="clk" num_pins="1"/>

      <!-- 8 BLEs (fle/ble4 = LUT4 + FF + out-mux) -->
      <pb_type name="fle" num_pb="8">
        <input  name="in"  num_pins="4"/>
        <output name="out" num_pins="1"/>
        <clock  name="clk" num_pins="1"/>

        <mode name="n1_lut4">
          <pb_type name="ble4" num_pb="1">
            <input  name="in"  num_pins="4"/>
            <output name="out" num_pins="1"/>
            <clock  name="clk" num_pins="1"/>

            <!-- LUT4 -->
            <pb_type name="lut4" blif_model=".names" num_pb="1" class="lut">
              <input  name="in"  num_pins="4" port_class="lut_in"/>
              <output name="out" num_pins="1" port_class="lut_out"/>
              <delay_matrix type="max" in_port="lut4.in" out_port="lut4.out">
                2.253000e-10
                2.253000e-10
                2.253000e-10
                2.253000e-10
              </delay_matrix>
            </pb_type>

            <!-- FF -->
            <pb_type name="ff" blif_model=".latch" num_pb="1" class="flipflop">
              <input  name="D"   num_pins="1" port_class="D"/>
              <output name="Q"   num_pins="1" port_class="Q"/>
              <clock  name="clk" num_pins="1" port_class="clock"/>
              <T_setup value="2.160000e-10" port="ff.D" clock="clk"/>
              <T_clock_to_Q max="1.426000e-10" port="ff.Q" clock="clk"/>
            </pb_type>

            <interconnect>
              <direct name="direct1" input="ble4.in"     output="lut4[0:0].in"/>
              <direct name="direct2" input="lut4.out"    output="ff.D">
                <pack_pattern name="ble4" in_port="lut4.out" out_port="ff.D"/>
              </direct>
              <direct name="direct3" input="ble4.clk"    output="ff.clk"/>
              <mux name="mux1" input="ff.Q lut4.out" output="ble4.out"/>
            </interconnect>
          </pb_type>

          <interconnect>
            <direct name="direct1" input="fle.in"   output="ble4.in"/>
            <direct name="direct2" input="ble4.out" output="fle.out[0:0]"/>
            <direct name="direct3" input="fle.clk"  output="ble4.clk"/>
          </interconnect>
        </mode>
      </pb_type>

      <!-- flat full-input crossbar: clb.I + all fle.out -> every fle.in
           (mirrors clb_t IIB: 18 ext + 8 feedback = 26 sources) -->
      <interconnect>
        <complete name="crossbar" input="clb.I fle[7:0].out" output="fle[7:0].in">
          <delay_constant max="5.735000e-11" in_port="clb.I"      out_port="fle[7:0].in"/>
          <delay_constant max="5.428000e-11" in_port="fle[7:0].out" out_port="fle[7:0].in"/>
        </complete>
        <complete name="clks" input="clb.clk" output="fle[7:0].clk"/>
        <direct  name="clbouts1" input="fle[7:0].out" output="clb.O"/>
      </interconnect>

      <!-- fc in_val=1.0 = FAITHFUL to the implemented connection_block: each
           clb_in is a full mux over all 4*W local tracks (any input reads any
           track). out_val=0.25 approximates clb_out injecting onto out_e only
           (1 of 4 dirs). Exact rr_graph->mux mapping is bitgen's job (E0-MAP3). -->
      <fc in_type="frac" in_val="1.0" out_type="frac" out_val="0.25"/>
      <pinlocations pattern="spread"/>
    </pb_type>

    <!-- ================= Ethereal DSP-T (mult_27x18: 27x18 -> 48 MAC) ================= -->
    <pb_type name="mult_27x18" height="1">
      <input  name="a"   num_pins="27"/>
      <input  name="b"   num_pins="18"/>
      <output name="out" num_pins="48"/>

      <!-- leaf: the $macc_v2 hard cell Yosys emits (alumacc). Combinational. -->
      <pb_type name="mult_27x18_slice" blif_model=".subckt $macc_v2" num_pb="1">
        <input  name="A" num_pins="27"/>
        <input  name="B" num_pins="18"/>
        <output name="Y" num_pins="48"/>
        <delay_constant max="1.523e-9" in_port="mult_27x18_slice.A" out_port="mult_27x18_slice.Y"/>
        <delay_constant max="1.523e-9" in_port="mult_27x18_slice.B" out_port="mult_27x18_slice.Y"/>
      </pb_type>

      <interconnect>
        <direct name="a2a"     input="mult_27x18.a"        output="mult_27x18_slice.A"/>
        <direct name="b2b"     input="mult_27x18.b"        output="mult_27x18_slice.B"/>
        <direct name="out2out" input="mult_27x18_slice.Y"  output="mult_27x18.out"/>
      </interconnect>

      <!-- fc 1.0/1.0 (ASSUMPTION E, revised): wide tiles need every pin to reach
           tracks; VTR's 0.15/0.10 (for its own wide tiles) left most of our
           mult/mem pins with no rr_graph fanin/fanout at W=12 (no routing
           channels pass the tall hard columns at this tiny channel width), so we
           connect all pins to the channel. Exact mapping is bitgen's job. -->
      <fc in_type="frac" in_val="1.0" out_type="frac" out_val="1.0"/>
      <pinlocations pattern="spread"/>
      <power method="ignore"/>
    </pb_type>

    <!-- ================= Ethereal MEM-T (mem_2Kx32: 2K x 32 sync RAM) ================= -->
    <!-- class="memory" lets VPR pack the $mem_v2 atom. VPR's memory-class
         machinery (ProcessMemoryClass) derives the data width from the
         data-class ports (WR_DATA/RD_DATA = 32) and auto-builds the per-bit
         memory_slice interconnect. We declare the tile ports to match the
         Yosys $mem_v2 model; the slice-level ports use VPR's canonical
         port_class tokens (address/data_in/write_en/data_out/clock).

         NOTE (ASSUMPTION G): the real $mem_v2 is dual-port (separate RD_*/WR_*).
         VPR's memory class is a single-address space abstraction; we expose one
         unified addr and treat RD_EN/WR_EN as enables. The $mem_v2 model's
         RD_ARST/RD_SRST (async/sync reset) are folded into the `ctrl` bundle and
         tied off in Phase-1 probes — full reset inference is deferred to the
         heterogeneous bitgen (E0-MAP3, not yet built). The tile container holds
         the class="memory" leaf below; VPR's memory machinery (ProcessMemoryClass)
         derives the 32-bit width from the data-class ports. -->
    <pb_type name="mem_2Kx32" height="1">
      <input  name="addr"    num_pins="11"/>
      <input  name="data_in" num_pins="32"/>
      <input  name="we"      num_pins="1"/>
      <input  name="ctrl"    num_pins="4"/>  <!-- RD_EN + RD_ARST + RD_SRST + spare -->
      <output name="data_out" num_pins="32"/>
      <clock  name="clk"     num_pins="1"/>

      <!-- leaf carrying the $mem_v2 blif_model. NOT class="memory": VPR's memory
           class (ProcessMemoryClass) NILS the leaf's model and rebuilds it as a
           canonical single-port memory_slice, which cannot represent Yosys's
           dual-port $mem_v2 (RD_*/WR_*). So we model it as a plain sequential
           leaf whose ports match the $mem_v2 model one-to-one; the packer places
           the $mem_v2 atom here directly. -->
      <pb_type name="mem_2Kx32_slice" blif_model=".subckt $mem_v2" num_pb="1">
        <input  name="WR_EN"   num_pins="32"/>
        <input  name="WR_ADDR" num_pins="11"/>
        <input  name="WR_DATA" num_pins="32"/>
        <input  name="RD_EN"   num_pins="1"/>
        <input  name="RD_ADDR" num_pins="11"/>
        <input  name="RD_ARST" num_pins="1"/>
        <input  name="RD_SRST" num_pins="1"/>
        <output name="RD_DATA" num_pins="32"/>
        <clock  name="WR_CLK"  num_pins="1"/>
        <clock  name="RD_CLK"  num_pins="1"/>
        <T_setup value="509e-12" port="mem_2Kx32_slice.WR_EN" clock="WR_CLK"/>
        <T_setup value="509e-12" port="mem_2Kx32_slice.WR_ADDR" clock="WR_CLK"/>
        <T_setup value="509e-12" port="mem_2Kx32_slice.WR_DATA" clock="WR_CLK"/>
        <T_setup value="509e-12" port="mem_2Kx32_slice.RD_EN" clock="RD_CLK"/>
        <T_setup value="509e-12" port="mem_2Kx32_slice.RD_ADDR" clock="RD_CLK"/>
        <T_setup value="509e-12" port="mem_2Kx32_slice.RD_ARST" clock="RD_CLK"/>
        <T_setup value="509e-12" port="mem_2Kx32_slice.RD_SRST" clock="RD_CLK"/>
        <T_clock_to_Q max="1.234e-9" port="mem_2Kx32_slice.RD_DATA" clock="RD_CLK"/>
      </pb_type>

      <interconnect>
        <!-- single tile clk drives both write & read clocks (ASSUMPTION G) -->
        <direct name="wr_clk" input="mem_2Kx32.clk" output="mem_2Kx32_slice.WR_CLK"/>
        <direct name="rd_clk" input="mem_2Kx32.clk" output="mem_2Kx32_slice.RD_CLK"/>
        <direct name="addr"   input="mem_2Kx32.addr"    output="mem_2Kx32_slice.WR_ADDR"/>
        <direct name="raddr"  input="mem_2Kx32.addr"    output="mem_2Kx32_slice.RD_ADDR"/>
        <direct name="wdata"  input="mem_2Kx32.data_in" output="mem_2Kx32_slice.WR_DATA"/>
        <direct name="we"     input="mem_2Kx32.we"      output="mem_2Kx32_slice.WR_EN[0:0]"/>
        <direct name="rd_en"   input="mem_2Kx32.ctrl[0:0]" output="mem_2Kx32_slice.RD_EN"/>
        <direct name="rd_arst" input="mem_2Kx32.ctrl[1:1]" output="mem_2Kx32_slice.RD_ARST"/>
        <direct name="rd_srst" input="mem_2Kx32.ctrl[2:2]" output="mem_2Kx32_slice.RD_SRST"/>
        <direct name="rdata"  input="mem_2Kx32_slice.RD_DATA" output="mem_2Kx32.data_out"/>
      </interconnect>

      <!-- fc 1.0/1.0: see the mult_27x18 fc note (ASSUMPTION E, revised). -->
      <fc in_type="frac" in_val="1.0" out_type="frac" out_val="1.0"/>
      <pinlocations pattern="spread"/>
      <power method="ignore"/>
    </pb_type>

  </complexblocklist>
</architecture>
